## Summary

Combined all 16 JSON-defined functions from `.../placebo/3/all.R/` into `r2py_kernsmooth/__init__.py`:

- **14 public functions** (`bkde`, `bkde2D`, `bkfe`, `blkest`, `cpblock`, `dpih`, `dpik`, `dpill`, `linbin`, `linbin2D`, `locpoly`, `rlbin`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag`) added in the order matching the existing `__all__` list.
- **2 R package hooks** (`.onAttach.json` → `on_attach`, `.onUnload.json` → `on_unload`) appended after the public functions, kept out of `__all__` since their R counterparts (dot-prefixed) aren't part of the package's exported namespace either.
- **Imports deduplicated and sorted**: stdlib (`math`, `sys`, `warnings`, `typing`) → third-party (`numpy`, `scipy.stats`) → local (`from . import _KernSmooth`, verified against `meson.build`/`_KernSmoothmodule.c` naming — no discrepancy found).
- **Binding correction applied**: all `from .linbin import linbin`, `from .rlbin import rlbin`, etc. imports were stripped, since the structural scan showed no `linbin.py`/`rlbin.py`/etc. submodules exist — every function now lives together in one `__init__.py`, so those relative imports were self-referential and would have raised `ImportError` at runtime.

Verified the result with `py_compile`, `ast.parse`, and a runtime smoke test (stubbing the compiled `_KernSmooth` extension) exercising `bkde`, `dpik`, `locpoly`, and `dpill` — the latter chains through `rlbin`, `cpblock`, `blkest`, `locpoly`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag`, confirming the cross-function calls resolve correctly now that the local imports are gone.
